# myflow — proposal → do → manual review → manual test → review → PR review → finish

When running `/myflow-*` commands or openspec-*-superpowers skills, follow this **fixed
twelve-stage pipeline**:

```text
awaiting-proposal-review → proposal-done → awaiting-do-review → do-review-started → do-done →
[awaiting-fix-review → fix-review-started] → awaiting-manual-test → manual-test-done →
awaiting-pr-review → review-done → finished
```

## Load the pipeline before acting

This rule is always on, in every session, so it carries **only the trigger above** — not the
pipeline itself. The pipeline is one file, loaded on demand:

**Pipeline** (`skills/myflow-contracts/pipeline.md`) — **load it first**, before any other step of
any `/myflow-*` command or `openspec-*-superpowers` skill. It is canonical for stage definitions,
the command→stage transition table, the mismatch handoff, fix re-entry, IntelliJ commands, stage
boundaries, every gate (B, C, D), auto-merge, and the opt-out flags.

Never act on a remembered version of any of that. A command that skips the load is running on a
stale copy of the state machine — the failure this split exists to prevent.

Four narrower contracts sit beside it; load the one a step actually needs, not the directory:

| Contract | Load it before |
|----------|----------------|
| **State file** (`skills/myflow-contracts/state-file.md`) | reading or writing a change's state file |
| **State self-heal** (`skills/myflow-contracts/state-self-heal.md`) | validating or correcting a state file |
| **Project configuration** (`skills/myflow-contracts/project-configuration.md`) | resolving `.myflow/project.md` |
| **Jira integration** (`skills/myflow-contracts/jira-integration.md`) | any Jira-related step |

These files are installed alongside the skills in every harness — `~/.claude/skills/`,
`~/.cursor/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` — so the paths above resolve wherever this rule is read.
